& [CoreProtocolProof] is eight integration tests
  + [equivalence] is direct query result exactly equals protocol query result
  + [inspection] is fabric, package, certificate, and semantic-unit state projected only after admission
  + [trust] is expected-package mismatch, environment substitution, and stale package visibly fail as trust
  + [binding] is caller, purpose, request, operation, environment, and package identities bound
  + [machine_form] is request, environment, and response deterministic JSON round trips
  + [strict_schema] is unknown root, nested query, and environment fields rejected
  + [exit_classes] is every numeric class fixed and nonoverlapping
  + [caller_verifier] is valid responses accepted while changed meaning, environment proof, exit status, continuation, or fault projection are rejected
  + [source_inspection] is semantic-unit inspection binds its exact quote to the signed source-document digest
  + [inspection_digest] is every successful inspect result recomputably digest-bound and a changed metric without a recomputed digest is rejected
  + [environment_verifier] is valid output exactly equals deterministic re-execution against the pinned environment while a changed metric plus recomputed digest is rejected

& [SubprocessProof] is five real executable integration tests
  + [query] is exit 0, empty stderr, one JSON stdout line, exact core equivalence, and caller verification
  + [inspect] is exit 0, exact core equivalence, caller verification, and byte-repeatability
  + [invalid] is malformed JSON, invalid semantic identity, and command-operation mismatch return JSON plus exit 2
  + [trust] is changed signed source returns JSON plus exit 3
  + [unresolved] is unknown term preserves the core query result plus exit 4
  + [policy] is unrelated caller package scope preserves denial plus exit 5
  + [semantic] is payload budget exhaustion preserves the core result plus exit 6
  + [file_input] is explicit request file semantically identical to UTF-8 standard-input operation

& [AuthorityBoundaryProof] is anti-injection evidence
  + [request_absence] is ProtocolRequest has no trust_store, packages, or trust-time fields
  + [environment_presence] is EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment exclusively owns trust_store, packages, and trust time
  + [environment_binding] is request expected_environment_digest checked before package admission
  + [package_binding] is exact expected package set and signed digest checked before admission
  + [admitted_type] is AdmittedPackage cannot be deserialized into existence and exposes only read-only accessors
  + [identity_type] is SemanticId validates every deserialized value and rejects invalid or over-512-byte identities
  + [continuation_type] is finish, query_or_reframe, and stop are closed protocol values whose status consistency is caller-verified
  + [scope_binding] is query package scopes must be a subset of the signed protocol request scope

